WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: uk

00:00:44.087 --> 00:00:48.813
Я дуже довго не був у
школі, тим паче на уроці.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.849
І прийшов, кажуть: «Ну,
англійська мова». Ну окей.

00:00:53.358 --> 00:00:59.473
І я дуже вдячна моїй мамі, яка мене
колись віддала із, там, з 5-ти років уже

00:00:59.673 --> 00:01:02.287
на мінімальні такі курси англійської мови.

00:01:02.391 --> 00:01:04.784
І я, насправді, полюбила мову цю.

00:01:04.975 --> 00:01:08.826
І вона у мене, в принципі,
в раціоні вживається,

00:01:09.112 --> 00:01:11.684
але є моменти, які можна підтягувати.

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:22.943
Hello, guys! It’s time for English lesson.
My name is Nataliia Liashko. Let’s start!

00:01:28.748 --> 00:01:31.625
And I would like to see my guests today.

00:01:31.736 --> 00:01:35.634
So, hello, Alina! Hello, Alex!
Alex, how are you today?

00:01:35.955 --> 00:01:38.099
- I'm well, thank you. And you?

00:01:38.258 --> 00:01:41.793
- I'm fantastic. Thank you very
much. What about you, Alina?

00:01:41.878 --> 00:01:43.192
- I'm okay, thank you.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:46.410
- You're okay, it’d good.
Let’s start the lesson.

00:01:46.561 --> 00:01:51.231
Today we are going to continue talking
about transport and we’ll add directions.

00:01:51.406 --> 00:01:53.489
Giving directions, okay?

00:01:54.171 --> 00:01:56.755
Let’s start with our homework.

00:01:57.205 --> 00:02:03.539
I asked you to rank the means of
transport from the slowest to the fastest.

00:02:03.855 --> 00:02:08.629
Okay, let’s just briefly discuss.
What do you think is the slowest?

00:02:09.035 --> 00:02:11.535
- I think tram is the slowest.

00:02:11.697 --> 00:02:16.328
- Amazing. Thank you very much.
Alina, would you like to add something?

00:02:17.546 --> 00:02:22.629
- To talk about the slowest or
to say what is after the tram?

00:02:22.747 --> 00:02:23.830
- You decide.

00:02:24.833 --> 00:02:28.083
- I think bus can be pretty slow too.

00:02:28.429 --> 00:02:30.419
- Okay. This is really good.

00:02:30.673 --> 00:02:35.590
Okay, what's next after tram,
bus? What's going to be next?

00:02:38.343 --> 00:02:42.341
- I think next one – ship.

00:02:42.615 --> 00:02:43.448
- Yeah.

00:02:43.909 --> 00:02:45.305
- Okay, agree?

00:02:45.392 --> 00:02:47.043
- Agree. For sure.

00:02:47.329 --> 00:02:50.945
- And what do you think
is the fastest? The top?

00:02:51.128 --> 00:02:52.128
- The plane?

00:02:52.702 --> 00:02:54.786
- Plane. Or helicopter?

00:02:54.871 --> 00:02:55.871
- No, plane.

00:02:55.963 --> 00:02:56.796
- Plane.

00:02:56.881 --> 00:02:57.798
- For sure?

00:02:57.913 --> 00:03:03.949
- For sure. Or it can be these Japanese
trains, which are going super-fast.

00:03:04.148 --> 00:03:07.592
- Super-fast, okay.
So, this can be possible.

00:03:07.704 --> 00:03:10.088
We have just train, a typical train.

00:03:10.173 --> 00:03:13.940
I don’t think this is super-fast. I
would agree with plane. Okay?

00:03:14.024 --> 00:03:14.857
- Yeah.

00:03:14.955 --> 00:03:17.860
- What do you think? Tell us.

00:03:17.945 --> 00:03:22.338
Let’s move on. How can I get from… to…?

00:03:22.545 --> 00:03:25.360
So, let’s have a look at the picture.

00:03:26.313 --> 00:03:31.982
We have railway station, a park,
cinema, tunnel, Jake’s house.

00:03:32.114 --> 00:03:34.534
So, we are talking
about Jake in a moment.

00:03:34.694 --> 00:03:38.277
And supermarket. Any
unknown words for you?

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:40.410
- I understand.

00:03:40.719 --> 00:03:45.369
- Okay, so, just an example.
I'm just checking you, okay?

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:52.075
How can I get from the supermarket
to the cinema? Can you help me?

00:03:53.017 --> 00:03:56.327
- With which transport
you can get – you ask us?

00:03:56.437 --> 00:04:00.548
- We don’t use transport here,
no transport on the picture.

00:04:01.048 --> 00:04:03.798
I think these words can help you.

00:04:04.225 --> 00:04:05.327
- Okay.

00:04:06.539 --> 00:04:11.787
- So, from the supermarket to
the cinema – how can you get?

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:14.920
- So, can I, please?

00:04:15.005 --> 00:04:15.872
- Yes.

00:04:15.957 --> 00:04:20.354
- So, you walk &lt;i&gt;through&lt;/i&gt; King Street

00:04:20.473 --> 00:04:23.140
and after you turn to the right.

00:04:23.533 --> 00:04:24.977
- Okay.

00:04:25.271 --> 00:04:29.943
- You are going &lt;i&gt;through&lt;/i&gt; the bridge.

00:04:30.261 --> 00:04:34.026
And on the right side
you will see the cinema.

00:04:34.111 --> 00:04:38.300
- The cinema. That was a really nice
answer, thank you very much, Alina!

00:04:38.428 --> 00:04:42.211
Okay, now we’ll focus on prepositions.

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:45.933
And we’ll come back to this a bit later.

00:04:46.062 --> 00:04:48.867
So, grammar time! Do you like grammar?

00:04:49.058 --> 00:04:50.465
- So-so…

00:04:50.568 --> 00:04:53.959
- Let’s do it…

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:58.870
- A lot of people say like Alex.
No, we don’t like grammar.

00:04:59.458 --> 00:05:03.344
Let’s try. Okay? It can
be difficult but let’s try.

00:05:03.447 --> 00:05:05.741
Maybe it’s gonna be easy for you.

00:05:05.924 --> 00:05:10.979
So, Prepositions of Movement. Let’s start
with number 1 – &lt;i&gt;to&lt;/i&gt;.

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:13.479
Repeat after me – &lt;i&gt;to&lt;/i&gt;.

00:05:13.593 --> 00:05:14.426
- &lt;i&gt;To.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:14.601 --> 00:05:15.434
- &lt;i&gt;Into.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:15.564 --> 00:05:16.397
- &lt;i&gt;Into.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:16.668 --> 00:05:17.501
- &lt;i&gt;Onto.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:17.747 --> 00:05:18.580
- &lt;i&gt;Onto.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:18.964 --> 00:05:19.797
- &lt;i&gt;Across.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:20.102 --> 00:05:20.935
- &lt;i&gt;Across.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:22.253
- &lt;i&gt;Along.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:22.406 --> 00:05:23.239
- &lt;i&gt;Along.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:23.834 --> 00:05:24.667
- &lt;i&gt;Out of.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:24.964 --> 00:05:25.797
- &lt;i&gt;Out of.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:26.443 --> 00:05:27.276
- &lt;i&gt;Over.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:27.436 --> 00:05:28.269
- &lt;i&gt;Over.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:28.436 --> 00:05:29.435
- And &lt;i&gt;through.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:29.563 --> 00:05:30.396
- &lt;i&gt;through.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:30.809 --> 00:05:35.543
- So, if you look at the pictures,
&lt;i&gt;over&lt;/i&gt; – if you have a bridge –

00:05:35.726 --> 00:05:40.390
what will you use with the
bridge? &lt;i&gt;Through&lt;/i&gt; or &lt;i&gt;over&lt;/i&gt;?

00:05:42.625 --> 00:05:46.801
- Probably, it can be
&lt;i&gt;over&lt;/i&gt;. Better than &lt;i&gt;through&lt;/i&gt;.

00:05:47.272 --> 00:05:50.390
Yeah, so, I made a mistake.

00:05:50.624 --> 00:05:54.332
- It’s okay, it was just…
We can use it in the lesson.

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:57.590
We test the students, then
we give them information,

00:05:57.757 --> 00:06:02.150
then we test them again.
It’s okay, it’s not a mistake.

00:06:02.317 --> 00:06:07.220
So, out of – this means
that you leave something - З.

00:06:08.675 --> 00:06:14.146
Okay. &lt;i&gt;Onto&lt;/i&gt; – on top. &lt;i&gt;Into&lt;/i&gt; – inside.

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:15.078
- Inside.

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:20.804
- Yes. Okay, &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt; – через,
тобто &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt; the street.

00:06:21.736 --> 00:06:28.256
&lt;i&gt;Along&lt;/i&gt; – вздовж. So, &lt;i&gt;along&lt;/i&gt;
the street or &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt; the street.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:34.738
It depends. Через дорогу
чи уздовж дороги. Okay?

00:06:35.181 --> 00:06:38.514
Now, let’s remember these prepositions.

00:06:38.628 --> 00:06:44.673
So, look at the words and I give
you 1, 2, 3 and you talk with me.

00:06:44.814 --> 00:06:46.897
We name them one by one.

00:06:47.408 --> 00:06:49.797
1, 2, 3!

00:06:50.006 --> 00:06:54.207
&lt;i&gt;To, into, onto, across,&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:54.382 --> 00:06:58.067
&lt;i&gt;along, out of, over, through.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:58.211 --> 00:07:02.907
Continue. &lt;i&gt;To, into, onto, across,&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:06.520
&lt;i&gt;along, out of, over, through.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:06.657 --> 00:07:10.889
Good. &lt;i&gt;To, into, onto, across,&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:11.009 --> 00:07:13.124
along, out of…

00:07:14.522 --> 00:07:18.629
&lt;i&gt;over, through… Through&lt;/i&gt;!

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:25.386
Okay, it’s gonna be more challenging. &lt;i&gt;To,
into, onto, across, along,&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:25.688 --> 00:07:28.060
&lt;i&gt;out of&lt;/i&gt;. Bravo!

00:07:28.145 --> 00:07:30.106
- … we just said it!

00:07:30.191 --> 00:07:31.033
- &lt;i&gt;Along&lt;/i&gt;?

00:07:31.137 --> 00:07:31.970
- No.

00:07:32.953 --> 00:07:33.786
- &lt;i&gt;Over&lt;/i&gt;.

00:07:33.871 --> 00:07:35.435
- &lt;i&gt;Over! Through.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:42.567
- Good. &lt;i&gt;To, into, onto,
across, along, out of…&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:44.213
- &lt;i&gt;Over&lt;/i&gt;!

00:07:44.313 --> 00:07:45.563
- Yes, amazing!

00:07:45.676 --> 00:07:46.509
- &lt;i&gt;Through&lt;/i&gt;.

00:07:46.613 --> 00:07:47.446
- Bravo!

00:07:47.546 --> 00:07:48.649
- Let’s remember.

00:07:48.847 --> 00:07:53.096
&lt;i&gt;- To, into, onto, across, along,&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:53.319 --> 00:07:57.720
&lt;i&gt;out of, over, through.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:57.911 --> 00:07:58.745
- Amazing!

00:07:59.533 --> 00:08:03.952
- &lt;i&gt;To, into, onto, across, along,&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:04.142 --> 00:08:10.707
&lt;i&gt;out of, over, through.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:11.046 --> 00:08:13.633
- Okay. Alina, can you try?

00:08:13.919 --> 00:08:20.813
- &lt;i&gt;To, into, onto, across,
along, out of, over, through.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:20.975 --> 00:08:23.516
- Bravo. Alex, your turn.

00:08:24.035 --> 00:08:30.959
- &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;To, into, onto, across,
along, out of, over, through.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:31.482 --> 00:08:37.508
- Fantastic! That was amazing,
wasn’t it? So, let’s move on.

00:08:37.632 --> 00:08:40.291
We have the prepositions
for you to remember.

00:08:40.387 --> 00:08:44.158
But I'm sure you know them
all. And we have 5 sentences.

00:08:44.325 --> 00:08:48.536
So, we need to choose the correct
preposition. Let’s go with number

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:52.786
1: Dad is putting sausages
&lt;i&gt;onto&lt;/i&gt; or &lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;into&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt; the barbecue?

00:08:52.988 --> 00:08:55.719
- &lt;i&gt;Into&lt;/i&gt; the barbecue… Or
no – &lt;i&gt;onto&lt;/i&gt; the barbecue!

00:08:55.831 --> 00:09:00.295
- Yes! Actually, when we have
a barbecue, we put them &lt;i&gt;onto&lt;/i&gt;.

00:09:00.557 --> 00:09:04.807
Number 2: She is swimming
&lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt; or &lt;i&gt;over&lt;/i&gt; the river?

00:09:05.349 --> 00:09:07.864
- &lt;i&gt;Across&lt;/i&gt; the river? Or no…

00:09:07.948 --> 00:09:09.249
- &lt;i&gt;Over&lt;/i&gt; the river?

00:09:09.361 --> 00:09:11.520
- &lt;i&gt;Over&lt;/i&gt; the river or &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt;?

00:09:11.623 --> 00:09:12.956
- No-no, &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt;.

00:09:13.041 --> 00:09:14.158
- Swimming &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt;.

00:09:14.309 --> 00:09:17.094
- Yes, &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt; the river. Number 3:

00:09:17.269 --> 00:09:22.349
The children are diving
&lt;i&gt;into&lt;/i&gt; or &lt;i&gt;along&lt;/i&gt; the sea. Diving.

00:09:22.613 --> 00:09:23.446
- &lt;i&gt;Into&lt;/i&gt;?

00:09:23.836 --> 00:09:26.461
- Yes, correct. Number 4:

00:09:26.724 --> 00:09:30.724
she is coming &lt;i&gt;through&lt;/i&gt;
or &lt;i&gt;out of&lt;/i&gt; the theatre now?

00:09:31.154 --> 00:09:32.815
- &lt;i&gt;Out of&lt;/i&gt; the theatre.

00:09:32.927 --> 00:09:35.167
- Yes. And number 5:

00:09:35.294 --> 00:09:40.575
Look! He is jumping
&lt;i&gt;out of&lt;/i&gt; or &lt;i&gt;over&lt;/i&gt; the fence?

00:09:41.309 --> 00:09:44.393
Do you know the word “fence”? Паркан.

00:09:44.541 --> 00:09:47.076
- Yeah but we are thinking… &lt;i&gt;over&lt;/i&gt;.

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:48.013
- &lt;i&gt;Over&lt;/i&gt;?

00:09:48.365 --> 00:09:51.674
- &lt;i&gt;Over&lt;/i&gt;. Yes, agree. &lt;i&gt;Over&lt;/i&gt; the fence.

00:09:52.639 --> 00:09:56.022
Well done! Now, let’s
have a look at this text.

00:09:56.197 --> 00:10:02.614
Jake is giving his friend directions
to his new house. And this is his text.

00:10:03.165 --> 00:10:07.112
When you come out of the
station, turn right. So, he is here.

00:10:07.364 --> 00:10:14.364
Exit and leave the railway
station. And walk … King Street.

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:17.623
What is going to be there?

00:10:17.767 --> 00:10:19.267
- Walk &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt; the…

00:10:19.982 --> 00:10:24.320
- These words can help you.
Once we already used &lt;i&gt;out of&lt;/i&gt;. Okay?

00:10:24.432 --> 00:10:25.658
- &lt;i&gt;Along&lt;/i&gt;?

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:28.272
- &lt;i&gt;Along&lt;/i&gt;? Alina, do you agree?

00:10:29.613 --> 00:10:32.280
- Do you remember what is &lt;i&gt;along&lt;/i&gt;?

00:10:32.365 --> 00:10:33.220
- Yes.

00:10:33.305 --> 00:10:34.388
- What is it?

00:10:34.473 --> 00:10:35.306
- Вздовж.

00:10:35.405 --> 00:10:40.384
- Вздовж. So, let’s see
how is it. &lt;i&gt;Along…&lt;/i&gt; Yes!

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:47.731
- Correct. So, you leave the railway
station. Walk &lt;i&gt;along&lt;/i&gt; King Street.

00:10:47.878 --> 00:10:48.711
- Yes.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:54.674
- Turn left on the River
Road. Yeah? And go?

00:10:55.099 --> 00:10:56.206
- … the bridge.

00:10:56.290 --> 00:10:57.123
- &lt;i&gt;Over&lt;/i&gt;?

00:10:57.244 --> 00:11:02.578
- &lt;i&gt;Over&lt;/i&gt; the bridge, bravo! We’re
already here. Walk … the tunnel.

00:11:03.068 --> 00:11:03.901
- &lt;i&gt;Through&lt;/i&gt;.

00:11:04.341 --> 00:11:10.200
- Bravo, &lt;i&gt;through&lt;/i&gt; the tunnel,
you are here. Get … of the tunnel.

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:12.623
- Get &lt;i&gt;along&lt;/i&gt;?

00:11:15.158 --> 00:11:16.575
- Вийти з тунелю.

00:11:16.724 --> 00:11:17.557
- &lt;i&gt;Out of&lt;/i&gt;?

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:24.064
- Yes. And until you get to
the Pane Lane, you are here.

00:11:24.203 --> 00:11:25.424
- Walk &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt;.

00:11:25.719 --> 00:11:30.858
- Walk &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt;. And my house is
right in front of you at number 12.

00:11:31.239 --> 00:11:33.120
Easy! Right?

00:11:33.252 --> 00:11:34.950
- You can miss it… Cool.

00:11:35.077 --> 00:11:38.312
- Yes! You can’t miss it.
It’s very easy to reach it.

00:11:38.527 --> 00:11:40.926
So, a task for you. Ready?

00:11:41.426 --> 00:11:44.760
Choose the correct preposition. Number 1?

00:11:46.329 --> 00:11:50.289
- John is walking &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt; the road.

00:11:51.263 --> 00:11:53.678
- Good, &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt; the road. Number 2?

00:11:53.877 --> 00:11:58.148
- &lt;i&gt;Over…&lt;/i&gt; He is going &lt;i&gt;over&lt;/i&gt; the river.

00:11:58.355 --> 00:12:00.105
- Good. And number 3?

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:02.785
- He is going &lt;i&gt;through&lt;/i&gt; a tunnel.

00:12:02.918 --> 00:12:04.101
- And number 4?

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:07.873
- He is going &lt;i&gt;out of&lt;/i&gt; the house.

00:12:08.107 --> 00:12:10.797
- Let’s check. He is going…

00:12:10.882 --> 00:12:11.715
- &lt;i&gt;Into&lt;/i&gt;.

00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:14.809
- &lt;i&gt;Into&lt;/i&gt; because there is
an arrow, have a look. &lt;i&gt;Into&lt;/i&gt;.

00:12:14.929 --> 00:12:16.279
- Ah, &lt;i&gt;into&lt;/i&gt; the house.

00:12:16.391 --> 00:12:20.941
- He is going inside. The door
opens and he comes &lt;i&gt;into&lt;/i&gt;. Okay?

00:12:21.108 --> 00:12:25.828
- Let’s move on. I suggest
you to play a game. Let’s play?

00:12:25.926 --> 00:12:26.767
- Let’s play.

00:12:26.871 --> 00:12:29.375
- We love playing games. You showed us.

00:12:29.486 --> 00:12:33.805
This time we are going to
play with a dice. This is the dice.

00:12:34.012 --> 00:12:37.738
And I want you to give me
examples with the preposition.

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:41.876
So, number one… If I roll
the dice and I have number 1,

00:12:42.067 --> 00:12:44.817
you tell me &lt;i&gt;“over”&lt;/i&gt;. &lt;i&gt;Over&lt;/i&gt; a what?

00:12:45.861 --> 00:12:51.474
&lt;i&gt;Over&lt;/i&gt; the fence, &lt;i&gt;over&lt;/i&gt; the bridge.
So, you give me an example.

00:12:51.594 --> 00:12:56.003
Okay? Like this. Just for you
to remember. For example:

00:12:56.202 --> 00:13:01.420
I have 4 and you tell me
for &lt;i&gt;along&lt;/i&gt;. &lt;i&gt;Along&lt;/i&gt; the street.

00:13:01.972 --> 00:13:06.696
&lt;i&gt;Along&lt;/i&gt; the river, for example.
It depends. So, ready?

00:13:07.112 --> 00:13:10.112
Who will start first? Alex or Alina?

00:13:10.463 --> 00:13:11.379
- Okay, me.

00:13:11.464 --> 00:13:12.372
- Alina.

00:13:12.456 --> 00:13:14.403
- But I'm a bit worried.

00:13:14.523 --> 00:13:19.624
- Don’t worry, no stress.
So, I roll the dice and 3,

00:13:19.831 --> 00:13:22.205
this is 3.

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:27.037
- &lt;i&gt;Across&lt;/i&gt;. I'm walking &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt; the river.

00:13:27.275 --> 00:13:33.081
- Bravo, one point to
you. Alex, ready? And 2.

00:13:34.148 --> 00:13:35.898
- &lt;i&gt;Through&lt;/i&gt; the tunnel.

00:13:36.212 --> 00:13:40.178
- Yes. Can you walk &lt;i&gt;through&lt;/i&gt; the
tunnel or you go &lt;i&gt;through&lt;/i&gt; the tunnel,

00:13:40.337 --> 00:13:42.513
or you drive &lt;i&gt;through&lt;/i&gt; the tunnel?

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:43.513
- I drive…

00:13:43.673 --> 00:13:47.194
- Drive, fantastic. Okay,
Alina, it’s your turn.

00:13:47.305 --> 00:13:50.609
I roll the dice. 6.

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:57.472
- &lt;i&gt;Into&lt;/i&gt;. She's coming &lt;i&gt;into&lt;/i&gt; the cinema.

00:13:57.663 --> 00:14:02.132
- Okay, possible. So,
Alex, your turn.

00:14:02.608 --> 00:14:04.314
6 again.

00:14:04.521 --> 00:14:07.188
- She is going &lt;i&gt;into&lt;/i&gt; the house.

00:14:07.825 --> 00:14:10.671
- Bravo. 2-2. Let’s try
again one more time?

00:14:10.775 --> 00:14:11.608
- Yeah.

00:14:11.696 --> 00:14:16.032
- Okay. So, Alina, for you. It’s 2.

00:14:16.413 --> 00:14:21.006
- &lt;i&gt;Through&lt;/i&gt;. She is going &lt;i&gt;through&lt;/i&gt; this pain.

00:14:21.316 --> 00:14:26.348
- Okay. Dramatic. Drama, total drama.

00:14:26.634 --> 00:14:29.729
Alex, 5.

00:14:29.962 --> 00:14:32.509
- She's going &lt;i&gt;to&lt;/i&gt; school.

00:14:33.412 --> 00:14:37.729
- Good, possible. So, it’s
3-3. Again, it’s? We call it a…

00:14:37.814 --> 00:14:38.647
- Draw!

00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:39.613
- Bravo.

00:14:40.005 --> 00:14:41.211
- Draw!

00:14:41.497 --> 00:14:47.033
- Bravo, well done. Let’s move on.
So, we come back to this, remember?

00:14:47.123 --> 00:14:47.956
- Yeah.

00:14:48.107 --> 00:14:52.064
- And can you help me now to get
from the supermarket to the cinema?

00:14:52.168 --> 00:14:53.918
Let’s try with Alina.

00:14:54.448 --> 00:15:00.682
- Okay. You're walking
&lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt; the King Street.

00:15:01.727 --> 00:15:07.555
Turning to the right and
going &lt;i&gt;over&lt;/i&gt; the bridge.

00:15:09.702 --> 00:15:16.689
And after you turn to the right and then
you gonna see the building with a cinema.

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:20.758
- Fantastic, thank you very
much! Let’s try with Alex.

00:15:20.925 --> 00:15:21.758
- Ого.

00:15:23.235 --> 00:15:27.822
- So, I'm at the cinema and I need to
go to the Jake’s house. Help me please.

00:15:28.527 --> 00:15:33.694
- You must enter the cinema,

00:15:33.845 --> 00:15:35.911
then you must &lt;i&gt;through&lt;/i&gt; the tunnel…

00:15:35.996 --> 00:15:36.839
- Go.

00:15:36.923 --> 00:15:38.353
- Go &lt;i&gt;through&lt;/i&gt; the tunnel.

00:15:38.449 --> 00:15:44.548
- Go &lt;i&gt;through&lt;/i&gt; the tunnel.
Next you must &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt; railroad.

00:15:44.988 --> 00:15:46.488
- Pane. Pane Lane.

00:15:46.782 --> 00:15:49.474
- Pane lane and…

00:15:50.971 --> 00:15:52.221
- You're there.

00:15:52.313 --> 00:15:53.646
- You are there.

00:15:53.862 --> 00:15:58.303
- Yes, Jake’s house is there.
Fantastic, thank you very much!

00:15:58.494 --> 00:16:03.021
Now it’s quiz time. I'm gonna check you.

00:16:03.204 --> 00:16:06.159
So: Walk &lt;i&gt;over&lt;/i&gt; the bridge. Correct?

00:16:06.517 --> 00:16:07.350
- Correct!

00:16:07.670 --> 00:16:12.783
- Yes, correct. What about this one:
Turn left and walk &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt; the tunnel.

00:16:13.042 --> 00:16:13.875
- No.

00:16:13.960 --> 00:16:15.003
- No, it’s false.

00:16:15.114 --> 00:16:16.027
- It’s false.

00:16:16.202 --> 00:16:19.785
- Because we cannot
walk &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt; the tunnel.

00:16:20.127 --> 00:16:23.869
- Thank you, Alex. &lt;i&gt;Through&lt;/i&gt;
the tunnel, okay? And one more:

00:16:24.354 --> 00:16:27.252
Get &lt;i&gt;out of&lt;/i&gt; the tunnel
and walk &lt;i&gt;into&lt;/i&gt; the road.

00:16:27.339 --> 00:16:29.539
- &lt;i&gt;Into&lt;/i&gt; the road is not correct.

00:16:29.684 --> 00:16:32.831
- &lt;i&gt;Into&lt;/i&gt; the road, it’s not
correct. What's the problem?

00:16:32.966 --> 00:16:33.799
- &lt;i&gt;Over&lt;/i&gt;?

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:35.289
- No-no, &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt;.

00:16:37.196 --> 00:16:40.848
- So, there are two parts here.
Get &lt;i&gt;out of&lt;/i&gt; the tunnel, is this…

00:16:40.975 --> 00:16:42.953
- It’s right, it’s correct.

00:16:43.112 --> 00:16:44.724
- And the second one?

00:16:44.907 --> 00:16:47.241
- And walk &lt;i&gt;through&lt;/i&gt; the road.

00:16:48.896 --> 00:16:49.729
- &lt;i&gt;Over&lt;/i&gt;?

00:16:49.851 --> 00:16:50.883
- &lt;i&gt;Across… Over…&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:51.034 --> 00:16:54.130
- You just mentioned this word.

00:16:54.315 --> 00:16:55.148
- &lt;i&gt;Across&lt;/i&gt;?

00:16:55.307 --> 00:17:01.807
- Yes. &lt;i&gt;Across&lt;/i&gt; the road. You cross the
road and you go &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt; the road. Bravo.

00:17:01.966 --> 00:17:07.812
Thank you very much. And one more task,
just to remember all the prepositions.

00:17:08.074 --> 00:17:14.620
Who will be faster? Let’s start with
Alina and Alex, okay? Alina, ready?

00:17:15.679 --> 00:17:21.384
- &lt;i&gt;To, into, onto, across…&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:23.785 --> 00:17:24.869
Is it &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt;?

00:17:25.516 --> 00:17:26.349
- Yes.

00:17:26.484 --> 00:17:28.868
- &lt;i&gt;Across&lt;/i&gt;, yes.

00:17:29.572 --> 00:17:34.522
&lt;i&gt;Over…&lt;/i&gt; no, over is after. I
always don’t remember this one.

00:17:34.762 --> 00:17:37.040
- It also starts with A.

00:17:37.125 --> 00:17:38.737
- Yeah, &lt;i&gt;across&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;along&lt;/i&gt;.

00:17:38.822 --> 00:17:39.655
- Yes.

00:17:39.775 --> 00:17:41.400
- Okay, &lt;i&gt;along&lt;/i&gt;.

00:17:42.005 --> 00:17:48.370
Get out? No-no, &lt;i&gt;out of&lt;/i&gt;! &lt;i&gt;Over&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;through&lt;/i&gt;.

00:17:48.565 --> 00:17:52.177
- Amazing! Thank you very
much. Alex, can you do it faster?

00:17:52.392 --> 00:17:54.108
- Maybe.

00:17:54.302 --> 00:17:55.302
- Let’s try.

00:17:55.593 --> 00:18:01.376
- &lt;i&gt;To, into, onto, across, along,&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:01.654 --> 00:18:03.488
&lt;i&gt;out of, over, through.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:03.573 --> 00:18:04.540
- Yay!

00:18:04.683 --> 00:18:09.440
- Amazing. That was
really nice. And we check.

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:14.356
- … &lt;i&gt;Across, along, out
of, over. Along and out of.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:14.505 --> 00:18:19.070
- Everything is correct. &lt;i&gt;Along&lt;/i&gt; and
&lt;i&gt;out of&lt;/i&gt; – these are confusing for you?

00:18:19.198 --> 00:18:21.255
- Yeah, I'm bugging there.

00:18:21.382 --> 00:18:25.166
- Yeah, probably just the
pictures. &lt;i&gt;Out of&lt;/i&gt; – just &lt;i&gt;out of&lt;/i&gt; the box.

00:18:25.254 --> 00:18:26.753
Think &lt;i&gt;out of&lt;/i&gt; the box.

00:18:26.865 --> 00:18:31.340
- Yeah, &lt;i&gt;out of&lt;/i&gt; the box! And
I always want to say &lt;i&gt;get off&lt;/i&gt;.

00:18:31.524 --> 00:18:35.148
- Yes, sometimes it happens.
But when we talk about movement -

00:18:35.291 --> 00:18:39.645
&lt;i&gt;out of&lt;/i&gt; the box – this is for you the
trigger word. And &lt;i&gt;along&lt;/i&gt; the street.

00:18:39.730 --> 00:18:40.848
- &lt;i&gt;Along&lt;/i&gt; the street.

00:18:40.933 --> 00:18:45.787
- Yes. So, your homework. You
are organizing a party at your house.

00:18:45.872 --> 00:18:48.201
Write a paragraph, give directions

00:18:48.286 --> 00:18:51.294
from the nearest metro or
bus station to your house.

00:18:51.379 --> 00:18:53.545
And draw a simple map. Okay?

00:18:53.630 --> 00:18:54.463
- Okay.

00:18:54.548 --> 00:19:00.069
- There is a bell. Unfortunately, we have
to stop the lesson. Thank you very much!

00:19:00.154 --> 00:19:01.050
- Thank you.

00:19:01.135 --> 00:19:02.445
- Thank you, Nataliia!

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:03.784
- See you next time!

00:19:08.861 --> 00:19:12.322
- Всі ми колись хотіли,
навпаки, звільнитися від цього.

00:19:12.425 --> 00:19:15.347
Тому що це – 11 років ми вчилися,

00:19:15.443 --> 00:19:20.679
в нас намагалися вштрикнути всі ці
знання, які ми так тяжко приймали.

00:19:20.782 --> 00:19:26.835
Ну, я скажу, що зараз десь я би
хотіла мати знову змогу вчитися.

00:19:27.018 --> 00:19:29.268
Сидіти і поглинати знання.

00:19:29.413 --> 00:19:34.245
Тому що, в кінці кінців, як мій
батько казав: «Це пригодилося».

00:19:35.642 --> 00:19:41.883
Будем пробувати. Сподобалось. Дуже
класна вчителька і все так пояснювала.

00:19:42.084 --> 00:19:45.231
Технології! Мене
вразили технології. Дошка,

00:19:45.399 --> 00:19:49.815
пультиком там воно щось
переключалось, все так цікаво було.

00:19:49.908 --> 00:19:52.347
Комунікація просто
на фантастичному рівні.

